{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
By [G]yon bonnie banks and by [Em]yon bonnie braes,
Where the [C]sun shines bright on Loch [D]Lomond,
Where [G]me and my true love were [Em]ever wont to gae,
On the [C]bonnie, bonnie [D]banks o' Loch [G]Lomond.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O ye'll [G]tak' the high road,
And [Em]I'll tak' the low road,
And I'll [C]be in Scotland a[D]fore ye,
But [G]me and my true love will [Em]never meet again
On the [C]bonnie, bonnie [D]banks o' Loch [G]Lomond.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
'Twas [G]there that we parted in [Em]yon shady glen,
On the [C]steep, steep side o' Ben [D]Lomond,
Where in [G]purple hue the Hieland [Em]hills we view,
And the [C]moon coming [D]out in the [G]gloaming.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: G}
